    {
      "id": "d49b609c-bf2a-4d6f-989b-71f0ceb4a58c",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1824,
        1216
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 848,
        "height": 756,
        "content": "## 📉 Customer Churn Risk Scoring Agent – Automated CS Intervention\n\n### How it works\nEvery 6 hours, this workflow pulls signals from four data sources in parallel: product usage from your database, engagement scores from Mixpanel, NPS scores from your database, and recent support tickets from Zendesk. All four streams are merged into a single customer object. A code node computes a churn risk score per customer based on days since last login, engagement percentile, NPS score, and open ticket count. Customers above the risk threshold are routed: medium risk gets a personalised check-in email via Gmail; high risk additionally triggers a Calendly booking link, a ClickUp CS task, and a Slack escalation to the account manager. Every intervention is logged back to the database.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Connect **Postgres** to `Get Product Usage (DB)` and `Get Latest NPS Scores` — replace with your DB connection.\n2. Connect **HTTP Request** to `Get Mixpanel Engagement` — add your Mixpanel API key.\n3. Connect **Zendesk** to `Get Recent Support Tickets` — set your Zendesk subdomain.\n4. Adjust the score thresholds in `Calculate Churn Risk Score` to match your business definition of risk.\n5. Connect **Gmail OAuth2** to `Send Check-in Email`.\n6. Connect **Calendly API** to `Book CS Call` and set the event URI.\n7. Connect **ClickUp API** to `Create CS Task (ClickUp)` — replace the list ID.\n8. Connect **Slack OAuth2** to `Escalate to Account Manager` — set the account manager's channel.\n9. Connect **Postgres** to `Log Intervention`.\n10. Activate the schedule trigger."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "446a966a-1338-4cd1-83a7-68219563f25c",
      "name": "Section – Parallel Signal Collection",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -816,
        1216
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 780,
        "height": 1320,
        "content": "## 📡 Parallel Signal Collection\nFour data sources fire simultaneously every 6 hours: product usage + last login from your database, Mixpanel engagement scores, NPS survey data from your database, and recent support tickets from Zendesk. Running in parallel keeps the run time short even at scale."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ed0954ae-ee6c-4d5e-9256-d52b16a51042",
      "name": "Section – Signal Merge & Risk Score Calculation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        1216
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1060,
        "height": 1304,
        "content": "## 🧮 Signal Merge & Risk Score Calculation\nThree Merge nodes progressively join the four data streams into a single per-customer object. The code node then scores each customer: factoring in days since last login, engagement percentile, NPS score, and open support ticket count into a composite churn risk score."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fe227a5c-4f3d-4d15-8e0b-dec67c595f3d",
      "name": "Section – Risk-Based CS Intervention Routing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1104,
        1072
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1188,
        "height": 1496,
        "content": "## 🚨 Risk-Based CS Intervention Routing\nTwo IF nodes gate the intervention level. Customers below the risk threshold are skipped. At-risk customers receive a check-in email. High-risk customers additionally get a Calendly booking prompt, a ClickUp task for the CS team, and a Slack escalation to the account manager. All logged to the DB."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fa252a02-0a94-4ee9-92cb-b93f697d896e",
